    21|{"id": "fs_159", "fact": "花丝工艺 (filigree) is a traditional Chinese metalworking technique dating back over 2,000 years to the Han Dynasty, listed as a national intangible cultural heritage (国家级非物质文化遗产). A single piece can take months: craftspeople draw gold/silver into fine threads, then twist, weave, and solder them into intricate patterns. The Bilibili creator 雁鸿Aimee spent 200 days making a pure silver birdcage using this technique — posted May 18 2026, 15k views.", "source": "https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV-search:花丝工艺白银鸟笼 (Bilibili, 雁鸿Aimee, May 18 2026)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "persistent,culture,craft,Chinese,heritage,traditional-art", "confidence": 0.88}
