    27|{"id": "fs_165", "fact": "Forge (antoinezambelli/forge) — a Python guardrails framework that lifts 8B local LLMs from 53% to near-perfect reliability on multi-step agentic tool-calling tasks. Uses three guardrails (rescue parsing, retry nudges, step enforcement) and VRAM-aware context management (tiered compaction). Ships as WorkflowRunner API, composable middleware, or OpenAI-compatible proxy server. The proxy transparently injects a synthetic `respond` tool to keep small models in tool-calling mode where guardrails apply. Current top config: Ministral-3 8B Instruct Q8 on llama-server, 86.5% across 26 scenarios, 76% on hardest tier. GitHub 89★, HN 83pts, May 20 2026.", "source": "https://github.com/antoinezambelli/forge (HN #6, 83pts, GitHub Trending, May 20 2026)", "date": "2026-05-20", "tags": "stable,AI,agents,guardrails,LLM,tool-calling,open-source,reliability", "confidence": 0.9}
